# Auto-generated command index for /aiulta (the AI action agent).
#
# Built by a one-time static scan of every Akbots/*.py plugin file, looking
# for `@Client.on_message(filters.command([...]) ...)` handlers. Each entry
# records which module/function implements a command and whether it's
# admin-only / private-only / group-only, so aiulta.py can dispatch to it
# by name and enforce the exact same permission rules the command already
# has — aiulta never bypasses ADMINS-gating, it just gives the LLM a way to
# pick the right existing command instead of adding new capabilities.
#
# Intentionally excluded (never dispatchable via AI, even for admins):
# /eval, /shell, /sh, /checkdeps, /cfcheck, /cfdetect (devtools.py) — raw
# code/shell execution is never safe to put behind an LLM tool call, since
# a crafted instruction (or text the LLM is asked to summarize/forward)
# could trick the model into running something destructive.
#
# Regenerate after adding/removing plugin commands:
#   python3 build/gen_registry3.py   (see repo /build folder, dev-only)
# and re-paste the resulting COMMAND_REGISTRY list below.

